[{:db/id 17592186195921 :answer-field/correct 17592186195925 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195915 :answer-field/correct 17592186195920 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195909 :answer-field/correct 17592186195912 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-183325"] :question/problem "Describe the set $S={5,6,7,...,50}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS={x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers between $5$ and $50$ (including $5$ and $50$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,5\\le x\\le 50}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $4<x<51.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,4<x<51},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,4<x<51}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195926 :answer-field/correct 17592186195929 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186198770 :question/answer-fields 17592186195932] {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/04433330c0f32cd6616c3e165342849b54ff496f11e9335d904a59cba7d71d22" :answer/id #uuid "48979afb-5d74-5496-a277-2c845ad0d277" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{is even}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/9a407ed61fd36c140de8ee053b7c6ff1ce616fd9af5cbbd1ba28c020ed5ee381" :answer/id #uuid "4885f03e-bc75-5736-a212-aa5e911535d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\in Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/21dad0b6f30c9958af7869bda594038137b5f5dc3abb3bb6cdc830d7f6d27116" :answer/id #uuid "9872363f-9fe5-5649-a551-2d2cfa7563bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\in N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/53b1f84dcf10761a401cb01c88a4bb24fff5835471e7b5fb580b1c37e60e8035" :answer/id #uuid "9ec1448f-91b7-58b9-8b0e-94b4f5f0b536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{is odd}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/028ac5109360f12a5f01cfb7dd17bbd52854c23504b963912e2a9ba7b076721c" :answer/id #uuid "699bf6eb-29ba-5b54-a3c9-7ec84dcf1d91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57" :answer-field/id #uuid "60f657ba-ef18-5ccd-a35d-d8b347b7116c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/21dad0b6f30c9958af7869bda594038137b5f5dc3abb3bb6cdc830d7f6d27116" :answer-field/choices ["q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/04433330c0f32cd6616c3e165342849b54ff496f11e9335d904a59cba7d71d22" "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/9a407ed61fd36c140de8ee053b7c6ff1ce616fd9af5cbbd1ba28c020ed5ee381" "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/21dad0b6f30c9958af7869bda594038137b5f5dc3abb3bb6cdc830d7f6d27116" "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/53b1f84dcf10761a401cb01c88a4bb24fff5835471e7b5fb580b1c37e60e8035" "q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57/028ac5109360f12a5f01cfb7dd17bbd52854c23504b963912e2a9ba7b076721c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-183327"] :question/problem "Describe the set $S={3,5,7,9,11,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\,{{field-2}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,7,\\,11,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =5-3 \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,n\\ge 1$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={2n+1\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183327/field-2/ma-v1/0b20f213b275607dfc146774109e482cba23611e83342c1ee936e1a755499d57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728/field-1/3b4a62ec12096f6ae97aa20ab89d0c4ad3c5693cda39070717878640fd7d8c92" :answer/id #uuid "4d6621c4-a07c-571d-8823-fe693d8e0a02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3+3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "824fad63-0ebf-5007-91c0-2a7d48c090a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e07b471d-78a8-5913-9810-a3bf1ddb77c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183728/field-1/3b4a62ec12096f6ae97aa20ab89d0c4ad3c5693cda39070717878640fd7d8c92" :answer-field/choices ["q-183728/field-1/3b4a62ec12096f6ae97aa20ab89d0c4ad3c5693cda39070717878640fd7d8c92" "q-183728/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728/field-2/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "014ec205-d1c7-569d-991e-378843824737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "e643250c-67dc-5eba-96cc-e35bb05f062c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183728/field-2/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer-field/choices ["q-183728/field-2/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183728" :question/id #uuid "b6ca7f56-21b3-5216-a2b0-306b24a6b696" :question/math-academy-id "q-183728" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${1,\\sqrt{2}}$ given below.\n\n${1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{2},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(x-1)(x-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183728/field-1" "q-183728/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183728"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "476194df-0b1a-5976-8cbe-4dc5fc868140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183729/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b72edfe8-46d4-5502-8d98-484e0ba36565" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-183729/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183729/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "035d0891-ae01-544d-aae8-24dd4104ef0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183729/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "736ab067-9adf-54b4-a07f-0396ff269b17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-183729/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-183729/field-2/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183729" :question/id #uuid "b30719fb-e464-5870-9e0a-b27486e0ebd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183729" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-(-\\sqrt{3}))(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{3}x+\\sqrt{3}x-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{2}+0x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+0x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-\\sqrt{3},\\sqrt{3}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,2{x}^{2}+0x-6=0}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183729/field-1" "q-183729/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183729"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-1/30ab724c845c65b640d273c8e51a31006a85319d78d66465e9ec1a19d391a8e5" :answer/id #uuid "1b8a2176-6f37-5bd2-b468-b232ff66f4c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-1/6d62fe58916fec806d29b34850a3474a2a0d4fc4fb5b7c7c7327f0550609f740" :answer/id #uuid "49cc6f5a-fd37-5042-bedb-987180f36620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-1/579776c349e005b8d209b47be003eb94eb3df0caf9bb1321c0f4296636d03eb3" :answer/id #uuid "c29092af-c3a8-59ed-841e-9398c3d777b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-1/b8cbde4dfadbc2cd309c521a717aa7f7cc79b565aebfbef17a0c3a312a7b6445" :answer/id #uuid "18757baa-72bd-5947-aecb-1ed04c9032a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "25c44860-4495-5018-926b-91c176bb4aec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-183792/field-1/b8cbde4dfadbc2cd309c521a717aa7f7cc79b565aebfbef17a0c3a312a7b6445" :answer-field/choices ["q-183792/field-1/30ab724c845c65b640d273c8e51a31006a85319d78d66465e9ec1a19d391a8e5" "q-183792/field-1/6d62fe58916fec806d29b34850a3474a2a0d4fc4fb5b7c7c7327f0550609f740" "q-183792/field-1/579776c349e005b8d209b47be003eb94eb3df0caf9bb1321c0f4296636d03eb3" "q-183792/field-1/b8cbde4dfadbc2cd309c521a717aa7f7cc79b565aebfbef17a0c3a312a7b6445"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-2/4d0c358832890f4f0221d2542d1721c57f92cd229eaf0a284d49f62ed4f133e3" :answer/id #uuid "af8d7ffb-484d-5039-8a43-7172385ee56e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Q" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-2/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "47fe78dc-0b22-5f03-a3b8-34b48f8321d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-2/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "2e25ef17-f244-562e-b128-5b72672f2467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "db3d13d5-1db6-5d71-9635-7aa3e7ec7648" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-183792/field-2/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-183792/field-2/4d0c358832890f4f0221d2542d1721c57f92cd229eaf0a284d49f62ed4f133e3" "q-183792/field-2/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" "q-183792/field-2/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183792" :question/id #uuid "f8edf910-c411-534b-97f2-739a78146702" :question/math-academy-id "q-183792" :question/problem "Describe the set $S={2,1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{4},...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS={{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n2,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{4},\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{4}}{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183792/field-1" "q-183792/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9df722a8-2db6-5bb8-a69c-b81b33037ab2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183792"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
